{"role":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The website is served by the Flask app in `simplification-of-trajectory-streams/web/server.py`. From that directory:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python server.py\n```\n\nUse the venv interpreter because Flask lives there. Plain `python3 server.py` fails with `No module named 'flask'` unless you have installed `web/requirements.txt` into that Python.\n\n**What it does**\n\n1. Checks that `build/simplify` exists. If it does not, it exits and tells you to run `cmake -B build && cmake --build build` first. The site is not static-only: API routes call that binary.\n2. Reads `PORT` (default **5050**) and `HOST` (default **0.0.0.0**). Port 5050 avoids macOS AirPlay on 5000, which returns 403. `0.0.0.0` is for Docker/Cloud Run; locally you can set `HOST=127.0.0.1`.\n3. Starts Flask with `threaded=True` so a long Fréchet request does not block other endpoints.\n4. Serves `index.html` and the rest of `web/` at `/`, plus `/api/traces`, `/api/trace/...`, and `/api/frechet`.\n\nThen open **http://127.0.0.1:5050**.\n\n**Overrides**\n\n```bash\nPORT=8080 HOST=127.0.0.1 .venv/bin/python server.py\n```\n\n**Personal page**\n\nTo serve the projects page and this visualizer together:\n\n```bash\n./scripts/dev.sh\n```\n\nfrom `personal-page`. That starts `python3 -m http.server` on **8765** for the static site, and the Flask app on **5050** if the SOTS repo is next to it."}]}}
